  "body": "Found during the #2774 work (held commits 8f6e59d1e + 815075be7 on `FlamingFireCoding:issue/2774-rotary-heights`), read against `origin/main` behaviour. Found by a test, not confirmed by a machine run.\n\n## What happens\n\nFor a Rotary Parallel operation with a radial cut band (radial heights stated as radii about the rotary axis, band 4.0..5.5 on an r6 bar), the app verifier refuses the generated path:\n\n```\nEnvelope { at: 38, gouge_mm: 1.544, rest_mm: 0.096 }\n```\n\nThe retip read overestimates the kept cut's clearance where the skin slants: the real tool pose dips below the model on the banded parallel path. The verdict correctly blocks the post, so a legal program is refused, not a gouge posted.\n\n## What the fix needs\n\nA re-read of the retip convention against the verifier's real-envelope law, for every banded path. It changes posted G-code, so it sits above the safety floor.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The retip read and the verifier's envelope read agree on the kept cut's clearance for slanted skins.\n- `rotary_verify::the_stated_radial_heights_move_the_generated_path` is green without weakening the envelope law.\n- The banded path posts or refuses with a correct verdict.\n\nPart of #2774 (the heights-as-radii feature stays held until this lands).\n",
